{
    "background_story": "Claire was a historian with a passion for uncovering the secrets of the American West. She spent years researching the infamous McAlester Prison in Oklahoma, fascinated by its rich history and notorious inmates. As she delved deeper into the prison's past, Claire became determined to share its stories with the world. She wrote a bestselling book about the prison's most infamous escapees and even led guided tours of the facility. Claire's work helped put McAlester on the map, attracting tourists and history buffs from across the country. Her dedication to preserving the prison's legacy earned her the respect of the local community, and she became known as the 'McAlester Historian.' Claire's love for the prison's history was contagious, inspiring a new generation of researchers and enthusiasts to explore the fascinating world of McAlester.",
